Parity scope (read from the web source end-to-end): DraftRecoveryBanner is a PURE presentational
notice whose only data dependency is `useTranslation`. It fetches nothing, so the web source has no
loading / error / stale / offline branches. Its actual render branches — all reproduced + tested —
are prop-driven:
  - `!hasDraft || dismissed`              -> renders nothing  (.hidden phase / web `return null`)
  - `hasDraft && !dismissed`              -> the info banner  (.visible)
  - `itemNoun ? restoredItem : restored`  -> two message variants
  - `draftSavedAt ? formatRelativeTime : t('draft.unknownTime')` -> Just now / Nm / Nh / locale date
                                              / "a moment ago"
